The problem is that '.' is recognizable as a direction, while '>' seems 
more like a action key -- 'take the stairs'. That's how I (and apparently 
other people) were thinking of it when trying to figure out how to dig pits. 
Maybe whoever does that sort of thing should change the help file to list 
directions as hjklyubn<>. or something, so people know that '>' was intended 
as a direction key.

